WEBVTT

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:10.490
The deal went perfectly, Mr. President.

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:14.170
You'll be able to see the shine of Little Comet 
for yourself as early as tomorrow.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.010
What are you doing? Get moving!

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:25.020
...But Sir...

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.790
Would you mind showing me some ID?

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:33.530
Can't you see those flags?

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:37.030
I'm the Ambassador 
to the Maranda Republic!

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:39.190
...You are interfering with diplomatic...

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:42.740
Oh, I'm sorry. How careless of me.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:43.660
Mr. Ambassador!

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:07.860
What are you doing?!

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.640
That's a foreign diplomat's car!

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:12.110
Move it!

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:34.000
Just a straight shot 
to the treasure from here.

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:39.450
"Queen Marta, World-Renowned Singer 
...from East Doroa, Assassinated in West Doroa"...

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:43.600
"Non-Aggression Pact between East and West 
...Broken, National Relations Tenuous"?

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:45.620
How stupid can you get?

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:51.150
Is West Doroa <i>trying</i> to make an enemy out of 
the entire world by breaking that peace treaty?

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.930
Who knows what they're thinking.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:57.530
I just feel sorry for the citizens getting caught 
in the middle of all this divided-nation crap.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.120
What's wrong?

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.450
You still hung up on that?

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.800
It was my job to protect her.

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:04.020
That's all.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.540
It's not how I'd wanna 
go out, that's for sure.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:16.800
This looks like quite the dangerous place.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.040
What'd you expect?

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:23.550
East Doroa's got the most efficient criminal justice 
system in the world. It's a veritable utopia.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:27.970
That'd explain why it's packed with 
so many ritzy mansions and embassies.

00:03:27.970 --> 00:03:29.810
A thief's paradise, eh?

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:32.680
I just hope this job goes well.

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:52.080
And the case?

00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:02.740
Go on in.

00:04:20.990 --> 00:04:23.280
Thanks for coming all this way.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.210
Sure. And the reason for my travels?

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:26.240
Right this way.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:35.070
This is Little Comet, the shard of the comet said 
to have landed in East Doroa in the Middle Ages.

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:39.500
East Doroa must have no taste if they're 
willing to hand over such a treasure so easily.

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:43.050
It just goes to show how much 
they are compelled by their other desires.

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:43.940
...You're referring to...

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:46.410
...West Doroa, of course....

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:51.340
For our part, we're supplying them 
with the means to enrich uranium.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:55.160
It's not hard to imagine 
what they plan to do with it.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:56.660
How foolish.

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:02.630
As you know, the Maranda Republic is merely a neutral 
third party, selling weapons to those who seek them.

00:05:02.630 --> 00:05:07.390
How they are used is of no concern to us.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:08.380
Fair enough.

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:09.160
Now, then.

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:12.020
Why don't you try holding it for yourself?

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:15.180
Here's the keypad. 
All you have to do is enter the code.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:24.000
Guess they're onto us.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.620
Is something the matter?

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:34.870
Who the hell are you?!

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.850
What're you doing, Jigen?

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:42.020
He hadn't told me the code yet.

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:43.640
There ain't time for chit-chat!

00:05:43.640 --> 00:05:44.440
We're leaving.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.700
Well, that didn't take very long. 
...I don't think we slipped up anywhere, though...

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.480
Guess this is our only way out.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:51.780
After you, then.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:55.290
Crap!

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:02.970
Damn!

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:04.030
That was close!

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:08.430
My, my. They certainly are swift here.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:09.850
What's our play?

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:10.720
This way!

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:44.170
What's going on?

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.460
...It's like they know our every move...

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:56.550
Lupin.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:01.810
Those are civilians' cars, you know.

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:04.250
You really think I'd stoop that low?

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:06.820
We ain't getting outta here 
without <i>some</i> sort of ride.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.110
If you insist!

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:25.060
One.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:33.760
Jigen!

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.920
...Son of a...

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.140
Him?

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:48.680
Two.

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:52.540
Lupin!

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:53.660
Damn, that stings!

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:56.660
Fuck!

00:08:09.670 --> 00:08:10.570
That bastard!

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:12.680
Who the hell had the balls to shoot at <i>us</i>?

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:16.730
I've seen a bullet like this once before.

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:18.180
What? Where?

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:21.060
Queen Marta.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:21.860
Huh?

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:37.880
You're telling me that was 
the guy who killed Queen Marta?

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:40.120
...Can't say for sure, but...

00:09:42.800 --> 00:09:44.140
How'd they find us?

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.790
Guess that reputation ain't a fluke.

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:47.730
Let's go.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.390
Go where?

00:09:49.390 --> 00:09:51.860
There's something I have to check.

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.320
What're you looking for here, Jigen?

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:03.490
I thought so.

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:10.130
Are you a ghost or something?!

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:13.340
I've heard rumors about this.

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:18.310
They say there's an assassin named Jael Okuzaki 
who makes graves for his targets before offing them.

00:10:18.820 --> 00:10:22.850
He never moves of his own accord. 
Only on his client's orders.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.350
Never heard of him.

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.820
What sorta guy is he?

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:27.660
There's not much intel out there.

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:32.720
No surprise, since none of his marks 
have lived to tell their tales.

00:10:33.310 --> 00:10:36.600
I'm only sure of two things: 
He's confident in his skills,

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:40.870
and he rolls a die to choose how many 
bullets he'll use to kill each target.

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:44.210
Revelry.

00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:45.560
Gratification.

00:10:45.560 --> 00:10:46.400
Victory.

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:48.300
The hell are you goin' on about?

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:51.700
That's what parsley means in the language 
of flowers. That and "impending death".

00:10:52.690 --> 00:10:55.380
He certainly seems to enjoy his work.

00:11:01.870 --> 00:11:03.540
You gonna take him out?

00:11:04.500 --> 00:11:06.550
I can't just let him go.

00:11:06.550 --> 00:11:09.140
Or do you think I'd lose?

00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:11.280
No one's escaped his 
crosshairs before, right?

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.060
You can't take him on with that wound.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.650
There ain't room in this world 
for two top gunslingers.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:20.790
I'm thinking of my friend here.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:22.770
That's your first mistake.

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:25.650
We're business partners—nothing more.

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:26.960
Certainly not friends.

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:27.850
That so?

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:28.910
Have it your way, then.

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:51.490
It is an honor to have such a 
beautiful woman pay visit to our club.

00:11:51.490 --> 00:11:53.810
My, you sure know how to flatter a gal.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:56.950
This club is strictly for members only.

00:11:56.950 --> 00:12:01.710
We only accept wealthy, 
refined gentlemen.

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:03.570
No one will give you any trouble here.

00:12:03.860 --> 00:12:05.250
I'm glad to hear that.

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:08.940
Well, then. Please wait here 
until we are ready to start the show.

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:55.790
I finally found you.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.990
Your show is about to begin.

00:12:59.990 --> 00:13:02.550
My, that late already?

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:09.300
This is quite the quandary.

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:13.210
That book isn't meant for a lady like you.

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:15.440
Hey, put me down!

00:13:25.100 --> 00:13:27.270
You gonna kill me, Daisuke Jigen?

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:28.480
Lupin the Third.

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:30.310
How'd you know I'd be here?

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:31.530
You didn't notice?

00:13:31.530 --> 00:13:34.850
That was wild-grown parsley 
he left on your grave.

00:13:34.850 --> 00:13:37.840
It carried a trace aroma of anemones.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:43.920
There aren't many 
anemone fields around here.

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:44.670
Wouldn't you say?

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:45.720
Beat it!

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.640
I ain't interested in your help.

00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.680
Likewise, I'm not here to help you.

00:13:50.390 --> 00:13:51.930
I'm curious.

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:55.960
I want to know who hired 
Jael Okuzaki to assassinate you.

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:59.690
The men from the embassy who 
want their treasure back, obviously.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:02.530
Then why wasn't there a grave for me?

00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:04.050
Something's fishy.

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:06.320
I came here to find out what.

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:09.070
Curiosity killed the cat.

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.330
I could say the same to you.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:18.520
Looks pretty deserted.

00:14:18.520 --> 00:14:21.450
I guess it's not his base, at least.

00:14:27.540 --> 00:14:29.090
A gun workshop?

00:14:37.550 --> 00:14:38.980
Hurry up.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:39.980
Don't push me.

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:45.110
This room's full of comm stuff.

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:51.120
Hey, check this out.

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:54.080
I guess he wears a lot of hats.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:56.310
Seems pretty good 
with his hands, at least.

00:14:58.570 --> 00:15:01.610
Seriously? Nothing but identical suits.

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:03.000
Prada, huh?

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:04.980
Looks like you two have 
something in common.

00:15:05.880 --> 00:15:09.260
I've got a wide range of suits, 
from Givenchy to Fendi!

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:10.130
Is that so?

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:11.190
Is anyone there?!

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:13.430
Please, somebody let me out!

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:13.790
That's Fujiko's voice.

00:15:14.070 --> 00:15:15.700
Anyone?!

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:16.040
This way!

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:18.640
Can anyone hear me?!

00:15:19.890 --> 00:15:20.880
Over there!

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:23.110
Fujiko!

00:15:23.990 --> 00:15:25.240
Fujiko, can you hear me?

00:15:25.240 --> 00:15:25.980
What happened?

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:28.090
That voice! Is that Lupin?

00:15:28.090 --> 00:15:30.250
Did Jael Okuzaki come after you, too?

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:32.150
Who's that?

00:15:32.810 --> 00:15:38.000
I decided to do a show at a club, but I guess 
I wandered into a bit of a sticky situation.

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:40.720
What're you up to, Fujiko?

00:15:40.720 --> 00:15:43.380
How could you even suggest that?

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:46.810
And here I was actually 
trying to go straight for once.

00:15:46.810 --> 00:15:48.790
But I guess I couldn't escape my past.

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:50.270
I'm finally done for.

00:15:50.270 --> 00:15:52.650
Hey, now. Don't jinx yourself.

00:15:52.650 --> 00:15:54.030
It's the truth, Lupin.

00:15:54.030 --> 00:15:55.760
But don't try to save me.

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:59.260
I wouldn't want to 
see you go down with me.

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:01.020
Goodbye.

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:03.200
You underestimate me.

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:05.630
Who do you think I am?

00:16:05.630 --> 00:16:06.530
No!

00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:07.710
Don't come after me!

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:11.400
What happened to 
"you never know until you try"?!

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.940
Would you like to roll the dice, then?

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:16.410
Wait.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:18.870
I want to ask you something.

00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:20.910
Why do you have 
Fujiko under observation?

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.530
The woman is not my concern.

00:16:22.530 --> 00:16:26.170
I was simply performing an 
operations check on my device.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:28.420
Then why are you after Jigen?

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.980
Any motives are not my own.

00:16:29.980 --> 00:16:32.170
I just take out the targets I'm given.

00:16:32.700 --> 00:16:33.800
That so?

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.170
Looks like you've 
overstepped your bounds, then.

00:16:36.170 --> 00:16:39.890
A sniper's never supposed 
to get this close to his target.

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:41.930
And there's no man who 
can beat Jigen on the draw.

00:16:42.380 --> 00:16:44.940
You have made two mistakes.

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:47.770
First, you've assumed 
that sniping is my only skill.

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:50.940
And second, you have greatly 
overestimated yourselves.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.430
It's high time I rolled those dice.

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:53.450
By all means.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:58.160
You did me real good back there.

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:00.950
Allow me to pay you back in full.

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:05.700
You're using your left hand?

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.170
Very well.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:10.210
Draw whenever you wish.

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:24.890
Three.

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:35.700
Jigen lost?!

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:37.820
Of course.

00:17:39.920 --> 00:17:44.080
A gun as large as a .357 magnum 
has no place in a duel.

00:17:44.340 --> 00:17:46.580
Now, the time for requests is over.

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:51.090
The next bullet, 
Daisuke Jigen, will be your last.

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:53.530
You can't beat him like this.

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:54.590
We're getting outta here.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:55.710
Get off me, Lupin!

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:56.590
Shut up and move!

00:18:03.740 --> 00:18:06.540
Never thought I'd see 
you lose a duel, Jigen.

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:09.480
His gun's a small .22 caliber.

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:12.100
And it's been modified quite a bit.

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:15.990
Think you could beat him 
if you had a gun that light?

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:17.860
Spare me.

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:20.530
You sure you wanna 
be stubborn right now?

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:40.140
Incoming!

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:41.180
Is that him?

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:19.310
I ain't running away without 
getting at least one shot off.

00:19:19.780 --> 00:19:20.970
Go for it, Jigen!

00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:22.970
Damn!

00:19:22.970 --> 00:19:23.600
No luck?

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:31.190
Hold on tight, Jigen!

00:19:36.010 --> 00:19:37.940
How do you like <i>them</i> apples?!

00:19:48.910 --> 00:19:50.040
What's going on?

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:53.130
Wasn't he supposed to go by his dice?!

00:19:57.760 --> 00:20:00.890
I guess there's an exception to the rule.

00:20:00.890 --> 00:20:04.140
And how the hell was 
I supposed to know that?!

00:20:08.580 --> 00:20:09.890
Serves you right!

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:13.450
Still no good.

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:24.820
Yuck, what is this?

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:54.310
We finally threw him off.

00:20:58.620 --> 00:21:00.620
He's not gonna follow us out here.

00:21:00.620 --> 00:21:02.910
I'll get him back later.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:05.960
Yeah. Nobody's invincible.

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:08.610
...Lupin...

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:09.940
He's back.

00:21:09.940 --> 00:21:11.450
Persistent bastard!

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:39.060
Exquisite.

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:45.560
...Jigen...

00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:46.820
A dead end, eh?

00:22:01.410 --> 00:22:03.210
Where'd he go?

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:04.840
Up there!

00:22:09.440 --> 00:22:10.660
Damn.

00:22:10.660 --> 00:22:11.600
He's got us in his sights.

00:22:26.130 --> 00:22:28.860
If we don't make it to 
that warehouse, we're screwed.

00:22:32.940 --> 00:22:34.580
Then we'll just have to go for it.

00:22:34.910 --> 00:22:39.140
Hold it. We'll be sitting ducks 
out there if we're not careful.

00:22:39.140 --> 00:22:41.000
And I ain't ready to die just yet.

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:43.180
Trust me on this one, Jigen.

00:22:43.180 --> 00:22:46.500
Just relax. 
He doesn't know when we'll go.

00:22:46.500 --> 00:22:49.380
We run to the warehouse on three, okay?

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:51.950
That's not a plan, that's a gamble!

00:22:51.950 --> 00:22:53.470
I'm the one he's after, you know.

00:22:53.470 --> 00:22:55.870
Screw this up, and I'll haunt 
you for the rest of your days!

00:22:55.870 --> 00:22:57.320
Wouldn't want that, now would I?

00:22:57.320 --> 00:22:58.020
...Damn it...

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:00.220
Fools.

00:23:01.060 --> 00:23:02.020
It's over.

00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:05.970
Let's go.

00:23:05.970 --> 00:23:06.530
Right.

00:23:06.530 --> 00:23:07.650
One.

00:23:07.650 --> 00:23:08.900
Two.

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:09.530
Three!

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:10.030
Four.

00:23:17.020 --> 00:23:17.480
Jigen!

00:23:17.480 --> 00:23:18.000
Hey!

00:23:21.790 --> 00:23:22.500
Jigen!

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:23.920
Get a hold of yourself!

00:23:24.970 --> 00:23:26.180
Hey! Jigen!

00:23:29.270 --> 00:23:32.510
How does it feel to watch your 
friend die before your very eyes?

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:36.560
You have only yourself to blame for 
going through with such a reckless plan.

00:23:36.560 --> 00:23:38.940
Now do you realize how 
powerless you truly are?

00:23:40.560 --> 00:23:43.660
You've shown me that you 
know your way around a gun.

00:23:43.660 --> 00:23:47.420
But if you ask me, 
you're nothing but a gun yourself.

00:23:48.800 --> 00:23:54.660
Without someone to hire you and pull your trigger, 
you're just a worthless tool that lacks a will of its own.

00:23:55.190 --> 00:23:56.370
Be grateful.

00:23:56.370 --> 00:23:58.910
That is the only reason you are still alive.
